      },
      "text": "SOURCES OF LAW HIERARCHY (US):\n  Constitutional law          ← supreme; cannot be overridden\n       ↓\n  Federal statutes             ← enacted by Congress; preempts state law\n       ↓\n  Federal regulations (CFR)   ← agency rulemaking under statutory authority\n       ↓\n  State constitutions/statutes ← valid if not preempted by federal law\n       ↓\n  State regulations\n       ↓\n  Common law / case law        ← gap-fills where statute is silent\n       ↓\n  Contracts / private ordering ← parties can contract around default rules\n```"
    },
